# Deployment & Commit Identity — ZatPat IMS

## Hosting

This project is hosted on **Vercel**, which **auto-deploys on every push to `main`**.
"Deploy" = push to `main`. There is no separate deploy step or build command.

## Required commit identity

Vercel **rejects deployments** whose commit author/committer email is not the
project owner. Every commit pushed to `main` MUST be authored AND committed as:

- Name: `decrypter`
- Email: `oceanz.lounge@gmail.com`

## How to commit (do NOT change global git config)

Set the identity per-commit via env vars + `--author` so the machine's global
git config (e.g. a work email) stays untouched:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="decrypter" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="oceanz.lounge@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="decrypter" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="oceanz.lounge@gmail.com" \
git commit --author="decrypter <oceanz.lounge@gmail.com>" -m "..."
```

After committing, verify before pushing:

```bash
git log -1 --format='%an <%ae> | %cn <%ce>'   # must show decrypter <oceanz.lounge@gmail.com> on both
```

## Notes

- Never run `git config` to set a global/local identity for this — use the env-var form above.
- If a commit was already pushed with the wrong identity, re-author with
  `git commit --amend` (same env vars) and `git push --force-with-lease origin main`.
- Do not add GitHub Pages / other deploy workflows — Vercel is the single host.
- After deploy, bump `CACHE_NAME` in `sw.js` if static assets changed, so the
  service worker ships the update to clients.
